# Bytes exactly as written, on every platform.
#
# Several fixtures here exist *because* of their bytes — one file is CRLF
# throughout, one ends without a newline, one is full of combining marks and
# zero-width joiners. Letting git normalise line endings on checkout would
# quietly delete the thing each of them is testing.
* -text

# What GitHub's linguist calls generated.
#
# `PullRequestChangedFile` has no field for this — GitHub computes it for its
# own UI and does not expose it through the API — so `.gitattributes` is the
# part of linguist's answer a client can actually read. These entries exist so
# the review page has something real to read it from.
generated/** linguist-generated=true
data/package-lock.json linguist-generated=true

# And what it calls vendored, which is a different claim: not machine-written,
# just not this project's code to review.
binary/** linguist-vendored=true
